[options]
[A.]
<$Playsound,horn.wav>
                                         <h2>Destruction of Thunder City<a href="#mission15">~[IfortGump.46]</a></h2>
                                                       ~[IthunderBlocker.1]
<br>                                                                                  ~1~y<?!{sw_difficulty1}>HARD</?><?{sw_difficulty1}>EASY</?>~.<br>

<br>
<i>After you rampaged Rain City and sacrificed the Ambassador you were ordered on your final preparation attack of the lands of the Furies.</i>
<br>
King {sw_hades} has been preparing you for his demented plot against the ~[Imanabolt.0]~[Imanabolt.1]~[Imanabolt.2]Furies.<br>
Long ago, after the Furies created King {sw_hades} to control the Nimbian Underworld,
 his envy of them grew. Sure, he could leave his realm just like the others
 but only for a short period of time. Since King ~rHades~. can be killed in mortal
 form, he travels in spiritual form. However, he must cast a spiritual changing
 spell that will transform him after it puts him to sleep.
 <p>
There are 2 problems with casting this spell; his body has no defense while he
 is sleeping and it only lasts for just under a Nimbian day. King Hades has
 evaded his enemies by hiding himself really well while the spell is in effect.
 <p>
$Button=More,Tell,more

[more]
                                         <h2>Destruction of Thunder City<a href="#mission15">~[IfortGump.46]</a></h2>
                                                       ~[IthunderBlocker.1]
<br>                                                                                  ~1~y<?!{sw_difficulty1}>HARD</?><?{sw_difficulty1}>EASY</?>~.<br>
<br>
For over 1000 Nimbian years King Hades has been plotting his revenge on his fellow
 Furies for putting him in this dark Realm of Hades. Sure, it is named after
 him, but he can never leave like the other Furies can.
<br>
So, King {sw_hades} has waited and waited for that perfect ~[Ipriest.123]priest to come to him,
one that can carry out his plot and do his evil bidding.<br>
Then along you come - And his plot <i>awakened</i>!
<p>
Every Nimbian decade the Furies all get together in the Serenisphere to keep their abilities and
 skills keen. They travl there in mortal form, by transforming into regular
 Nimbian Priests.
<p>
During the last battle King Hades captured the Wind Fury and would not release
 him. He broke the first of only two Fury rules of engagement - He sacrificed
 him!
<p>
$Button=More,Tell,more2

[more2]
                                         <h2>Destruction of Thunder City<a href="#mission15">~[IfortGump.46]</a></h2>
                                                       ~[IthunderBlocker.1]
<br>                                                                                  ~1~y<?!{sw_difficulty1}>HARD</?><?{sw_difficulty1}>EASY</?>~.<br>
<br>
Now, when a Fury gets sacrificed outside of their normal form it doesn't kill
 them, it only traps them into the last form they were in. This is how the
 Wind Fury stayed for almost 10 whole years.
<br>
This is the year that the Furies battle. This is the year King {sw_hades} has
 waited for. For this year he will have the advantage, for he has you. Now,
 you are wondering what the second rule is - It is this: The Furies can never
 ally with each other in their 10 Nimbian year battle.
<p>
So, this is the last mission before you get to meet the entire Fury clan.
 However, before you can meet them for battle you must have all of the knowledge
 possible to even stand a chance. This is why you must attack Thunder City,
 to gain the rest of the knowledge. Good luck on your quest!
<p>
                        <a href="cmd:ShowTechnology,55"> ~[IfortGump.50] </a>                                        <a href="cmd:DoNothing,0">~[IfortGump.22] </a>                                 <a href="cmd:Tell,guideHades.overview">~[Ipriest.13]</a><br>
              <a href="cmd:ShowTechnology,55">Review Knowledge</a>                  <a href="cmd:DoNothing,0">    Let's Do It!   </a>                  <a href="cmd:Tell,guideHades.overview">Leave HELL</a>
$OnExit= ,PlaySound,golemMove2.wav
$Button= ,Tell,A.


